blockr.script bundles third-party JavaScript in two files:

  inst/js/blockr-script.js   the script editor
  inst/js/prose-block.js     the prose editor

Both are built with esbuild from the sources in tools/srcjs. The libraries
they contain are named, with exact versions, in package.json and
package-lock.json of the source repository:

  https://github.com/BristolMyersSquibb/blockr.script

Libraries bundled directly:

  CodeMirror 6 (@codemirror/autocomplete, commands, language, legacy-modes,
    merge, search, state, view) and Lezer
    Copyright (C) Marijn Haverbeke and others. MIT License.
    https://codemirror.net

  Milkdown (@milkdown/kit)
    Copyright (C) Mirone and contributors. MIT License.
    https://milkdown.dev

Libraries those two bring with them include ProseMirror (Marijn Haverbeke,
MIT), remark, unified and micromark (Titus Wormer, MIT), and lodash-es
(OpenJS Foundation, MIT). Of the 161 packages the lockfile lists for the
bundles, 157 are under the MIT License. The other four are under
BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, and "MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0". All are
compatible with GPL (>= 3), the license of this package.
